  "interpretation": [
    "Negative cross-entropy differences favor the named arm; no significance claim.",
    "The frozen no-adapter model is the shared zero-update baseline. All four arms start at the identical function with zero feature gates; seeds vary paired minibatch order and finite-budget coverage.",
    "Seeds share evaluation blocks; blocks are not independent experimental replicas.",
    "Pointwise has 768 trainable parameters. EMA and learned history have 1537; fixed history has 1536 trainable plus one frozen alpha scalar. No dummy parameters. History versus pointwise includes additional capacity; EMA versus learned history matches count but not initialization of the filter, mathematical prior, conditioning or compute.",
    "All history arms use independent local and history gates. GL uses Rust forward_history with K=32, step=1, initial alpha=0.5. EMA uses ordinary Torch operations with strictly-past weights (1-d)*d^(k-1), k=1..31, initial d=0.5, with d=sigmoid(logit_decay). Neither renormalizes truncated prefixes.",
    "Primary contrasts: learned history minus EMA for fractional versus ordinary mixing; learned minus fixed history for order adaptation; fixed history minus pointwise and EMA minus pointwise for each history-plus-capacity change.",
    "Complete all twelve 512-update runs and exact next-update continuation before endpoint evaluation. Development scores do not select hyperparameters, checkpoints or run length.",
    "Pride/Alice are reused exploratory endpoints, not untouched confirmation. Report all seeds and losing outcomes; do not claim significance or unique geometric advantage from a quality difference.",
    "CPU float32, frozen local GPT-2, full unpadded contexts, no KV cache. History resets at each 128-token block. Extra work and host transfers are not a throughput benchmark. Prior full-GL results remain a separate historical comparison, not extra independently rerun arms.",
    "This summary checks published receipts, not checkpoint contents or process termination.",
    "No speed or pristine-corpus generalization claim."
